<title>AUSTRIA: NIGERIA SAYS EVERYONE HAPPY WITH OPEC AGREEMENT.</title>
<headline>NIGERIA SAYS EVERYONE HAPPY WITH OPEC AGREEMENT.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1997-06-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nigerian oil minister Dan Etete said on Thursday that all OPEC members were happy with the producer group's agreement to freeze output quotas until the end of the year.</p>
<p>&quot;There are no protests, everybody is happy with the agreement,&quot; he told reporters at the end of the conference.  </p>
<p>Ministers also vowed to adhere to their output quotas.</p>
<p>Before this morning's session Etete had said that Nigeria was not producing above its OPEC-assigned quota of 1.865 million barrels per day (bpd).</p>
<p>A Reuter survey pegged Nigerian production at 2.18 million bpd in May.</p>
<p>The Algerian and Venezuelan oil ministers have also denied that their countries are producing above quota.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 713 2002</p>
</text>
